#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:7
#: a6ae1f393fd84f5c9af26a995aa16272
msgid "Archived: Landing Gear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:9
#: 8874de8768bd43338fef80c43b07f968
msgid "Copter supports retractable Landing Gear activated by a servo mechanism (like these sold by `Hobby King <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/quanum-600-class-quick-release-universal-retractable-gear-set-680uc-pro-hexa-copter.html?___store=en_us>`__). The gear can be manually retracted/deployed with an auxiliary switch. The gear will also automatically deploy during landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:14
#: e4035970bd4941e3be82071ce088d545
msgid "There is some simple logic controlling the operation beyond simply responding to retract/deploy commands from the controller.  If the system is booted up and the landing gear control switch is in the retract position, the landing gear will not retract.  This is done to prevent damage to the landing gear or airframe should the switch be accidentally left in the retract position on start-up.  In this case, the landing gear will not retract until the switch is first moved to the deploy position, and then back to the retract position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:23
#: f64360b45b4c4e15970b93ffad3f6c22
msgid "The landing gear will automatically deploy when the flight mode is changed to Land, during the final landing phase of RTL mode, and when a Land command is executed in AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:28
#: 1852926bb8af4ee6a605a6a2f923bce6
msgid "Support for landing gear was introduced in AC 3.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:34
#: 8a3e70acd34c4d948bf140894ea18a42
msgid "Connecting to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:36
#: f76b5fc0af904dc3921175aaa18430a7
msgid "Most retractable landing gear will require just a single PWM cable to connected to one of the AUX outputs on the back of the Pixhawk (AUX1 ~ AUX4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:45
#: 9f9aa2a80da64fca9c611c806df8dedb
msgid "The signal wire (usually white) should be connected to the lower most \"S\" pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:48
#: 4e14da936f1949b0bceab797a91e82b0
msgid "Setup through the Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:50
#: b2a4c9dcc65a4d84a1ddfa1db3100f58
msgid "Use the Mission Planner's Full Parameter List (or equivalent) to set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:53
#: db3705960e63482cb2a538123e437cd1
msgid "If using AC3.5 (or higher) set ``SERVOn_FUNCTION to 29`` \"Landing Gear\", where **n** is the number for the connected servo (e.g. :ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` for AUX1, :ref:`SERVO10_FUNCTION <SERVO10_FUNCTION>` for AUX2 etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:55
#: 222f4f67afc24ebf89b1e7ebf255919c
msgid "If using AC3.4.6 (or lower) set ``RCn_FUNCTION to 29`` \"Landing Gear\", where **n** is the number for the connected servo (e.g. ``RC9_FUNCTION <RC9_FUNCTION>`` for AUX1, ``RC10_FUNCTION <RC10_FUNCTION>`` for AUX2 etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:56
#: d8b60613f4704ef79d67b4757e7ef663
msgid "``LGR_SERVO_DEPLOY <LGR_SERVO_DEPLOY>`` — servo PWM value required to deploy the landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:58
#: ec64d6cbd9b94792b60b15cde4e5a864
msgid "``LGR_SERVO_RTRACT <LGR_SERVO_RTRACT>`` — servo PWM value required to retract the landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:64
#: cc0bc702b9b5433cbed1896f2ea2160b
msgid "MissionPlanner: Landing Gear Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:66
#: 6a5dcbdb4938407bba5fbbefdd127a05
msgid "Set an :ref:`auxiliary switch <channel-7-and-8-options>` to \"Landing Gear\" in order to enable manual control (i.e. set CH7_OPT or CH8_OPT to \"29\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:68
#: 7def43f00d454b2c9eea806f548fa84f
msgid "When the switch is in the \"low\" position the gear will be deployed, \"high\" will be retracted, \"middle\" is a neutral position that will not change the gear's state."
msgstr ""

